.","t_yest":"November 13 was a typical day","p_yest":"The high of <strong>38\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 40\u00b0F, and the record is 68\u00b0F (1999). The low of <strong>18\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Brainerd has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If Brainerd's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Brainerd has set <strong class=\"sig\">26 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 84 that chance alone would give, and <strong>114 record highs</strong>, more than the 86 that chance alone would give. The 1930s hold the most record highs of any decade (54). Brainerd's all-time high is 106\u00b0F, on July 10, 1936.","t_chg":"Brainerd has warmed, days and nights alike","p_chg":"Across 95 complete years: Brainerd's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.24\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.10 to +0.38), about +3.0\u00b0F since 1899. Brainerd's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.18\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.07 to +0.30), about +2.3\u00b0F since 1899.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 5 of 12 months. Highs rose in 4 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Brainerd's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.18 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 25.9 inches a year. The wettest year was 1986 (37.45 in); the driest, 2006 (12.68 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 5 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}